{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00551",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.46,
      "end_seconds": 10.85,
      "duration_seconds": 10.39,
      "text": "Right, Mr Gallagher. The booking note says 'contact of a TB case, wants checking'. Is that why you're here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.9,
      "end_seconds": 22.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.63,
      "text": "It is, aye. My daughter made the appointment. I said I was grand, but she wouldn't hear it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.65,
      "end_seconds": 28.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Good for her. Tell me what happened, from the start."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.65,
      "end_seconds": 43.57,
      "duration_seconds": 12.92,
      "text": "My father was diagnosed with TB last month. They told us in the hospital, and the nurse there said the family should all get looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.16,
      "end_seconds": 55.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.09,
      "text": "That must have been a shock. How is he doing, if you don't mind my asking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.03,
      "end_seconds": 68.1,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "He's on the tablets now, and he's in good form. Giving out about the hospital food, so he must be better."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.45,
      "end_seconds": 79.35,
      "duration_seconds": 9.9,
      "text": "Ha, always a good sign. And how about you? Have you noticed anything yourself, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.14,
      "end_seconds": 86.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "It's nothing really. I've a bit of a cough, that's all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.67,
      "end_seconds": 92.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "A bit of a cough. How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.69,
      "end_seconds": 104.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "Two weeks, I'd say. It's a dry sort of thing, and it's worse first thing in the morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.5,
      "end_seconds": 112.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Is it a dry cough every time, or do you bring anything up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.69,
      "end_seconds": 116.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Dry, mostly, it just tickles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.48,
      "end_seconds": 122.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else? Even something you think is silly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.17,
      "end_seconds": 131.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.92,
      "text": "My voice has gone a bit hoarse, since Monday. The wife says I sound like a corncrake."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.64,
      "end_seconds": 136.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "A corncrake, lovely. Is that the only thing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.05,
      "end_seconds": 145.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "I'm a bit tired in the afternoons, but sure, I'm not twenty any more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.86,
      "end_seconds": 156.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "Mm. Tired in the afternoons, is that new, or has it been like that for a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.79,
      "end_seconds": 166.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "It's been the past week or so. Maybe it's the early mornings with the lad's football."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.9,
      "end_seconds": 172.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Maybe so. Have you had any coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.99,
      "end_seconds": 177.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "No, nothing like that. Not a spot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.42,
      "end_seconds": 188.55,
      "duration_seconds": 10.13,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Let me ask about your general health. Do you have any conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.01,
      "end_seconds": 201.81,
      "duration_seconds": 10.8,
      "text": "I've an underactive thyroid, years now, and a bit of eczema on my hands. That's the lot of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.01,
      "end_seconds": 211.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "And for the thyroid, what do you take, and how much? Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.33,
      "end_seconds": 228.27,
      "duration_seconds": 14.94,
      "text": "Levothyroxine, every morning. Maybe 75 micrograms? Or is it 100? I can't mind, to tell you the truth. The chemist fills the little box for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.86,
      "end_seconds": 239.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.35,
      "text": "That's grand. We can check it on the system later. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.6,
      "end_seconds": 250.83,
      "duration_seconds": 10.23,
      "text": "My appendix out, when I was fifteen. A summer I'll never forget, I missed the whole of the county final."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.56,
      "end_seconds": 267.25,
      "duration_seconds": 15.69,
      "text": "Ha, a hard price. Now, I'm curious about something. Your father was diagnosed, and you've seen him recently. How much time would you spend with him each week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.23,
      "end_seconds": 279.67,
      "duration_seconds": 11.44,
      "text": "Oh, every Sunday for dinner, a couple of hours. And I'd drop in on Wednesdays. But since the diagnosis I've stayed away, only the phone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.45,
      "end_seconds": 289.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Sensible. Well, before I examine you, can I have the nurse give me the numbers she took earlier?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 291.38,
      "end_seconds": 302.64,
      "duration_seconds": 11.26,
      "text": "Of course, doctor. Blood pressure is 124/80, pulse 78 bpm, temperature 36.9 °C, oxygen saturation 98 %, and respiratory rate 16 breaths/min."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.71,
      "end_seconds": 314.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Ahhhh."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.27,
      "end_seconds": 327.33,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "Your throat looks a little red at the back, nothing dramatic. Now take some deep breaths in and out while I listen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.0,
      "end_seconds": 354.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.2,
      "text": "Your chest is clear all over, no crackles, no wheeze, and the air is going in well on both sides."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.9,
      "end_seconds": 359.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "So I'll live, is that it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.22,
      "end_seconds": 381.54,
      "duration_seconds": 21.32,
      "text": "I think you'll live for a good while yet. What I think is going on, and it is only my working view, is a post-viral cough, a lingering cough after a cold, with the hoarse voice that goes with it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.85,
      "end_seconds": 392.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "A cold? I never even had a cold. Well, the lad had one a few weeks back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.13,
      "end_seconds": 403.92,
      "duration_seconds": 10.79,
      "text": "That would fit. Colds are often passed round the house, and the cough can hang on for weeks after the cold itself has gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.59,
      "end_seconds": 409.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "And the TB? Does it rule it out?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.1,
      "end_seconds": 426.79,
      "duration_seconds": 15.69,
      "text": "I don't want you to feel I'm dismissing your father's illness, and being close to him was the right reason to come in. I'd just say that nothing I found today alarms me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.56,
      "end_seconds": 443.02,
      "duration_seconds": 13.46,
      "text": "That's a relief, I can tell you. The wife has been at me. Is there anything I should do for the cough itself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 445.53,
      "end_seconds": 458.31,
      "duration_seconds": 12.78,
      "text": "Plenty of warm fluids, honey and lemon is as good as anything, and rest your voice. Don't whisper, mind, because whispering strains it more than talking softly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 460.49,
      "end_seconds": 473.87,
      "duration_seconds": 13.38,
      "text": "And if you ever start to cough up blood, or you get fevers and sweats at night, ring the surgery that day, don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 475.18,
      "end_seconds": 480.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "I will, yes. I'd not wait with something like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 482.01,
      "end_seconds": 494.86,
      "duration_seconds": 12.85,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in two weeks, to see how the cough and the voice are getting on. The desk will give you a time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 497.29,
      "end_seconds": 502.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Two weeks, grand. Will I tell the daughter?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 503.56,
      "end_seconds": 511.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.31,
      "text": "Tell her she did the right thing, and that she's earned a cup of tea off you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 513.65,
      "end_seconds": 517.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "She'll be delighted. Thanks, doctor, thanks, nurse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 518.7,
      "end_seconds": 525.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Mind yourself, Mr Gallagher. Mind the puddle at the door."
    }
  ]
}
